SIXTH HOKAGE — ANBU AND ROOT REVIEW
Kakashi Hatake, Rokudaime Hokage — Internal Review Memorandum

As a former ANBU operative himself, the Sixth Hokage ordered a full
review of the village's black-operations apparatus:

Findings and Directives:
- The Root division, long operated in secret under Danzo Shimura, is
  to remain formally dissolved. No successor covert body may operate
  outside the Hokage's direct oversight.
- All standing ANBU cells to be re-registered and their standing
  orders re-issued under the current administration.
- Psychological support to be extended to ANBU operatives; the toll of
  black-ops service is formally recognized.
- Sealed Root operation files to be reviewed for crimes committed in
  the village's name (see root_operation_files, classified).

The Sixth Hokage assumed office in a period of reconstruction and
reconciliation. By order of Kakashi Hatake.
